WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:16.490
woke up on Saturday morning with a big smile on my face.

2
00:00:17.411 --> 00:00:18.811
What was I smiling about?

3
00:00:19.212 --> 00:00:19.772
I wondered.

4
00:00:20.492 --> 00:00:21.753
Then I remembered.

5
00:00:22.593 --> 00:00:25.594
Today I was going to move into my own room!

6
00:00:26.535 --> 00:00:29.696
I'd never have to share a room with my brother, Tate, again.

7
00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:32.825
I went into the kitchen.

8
00:00:33.705 --> 00:00:36.607
My mom had left a note that said she was grocery shopping.

9
00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:41.871
I ate breakfast and then went back to our room.

10
00:00:42.491 --> 00:00:43.812
By now Tate was awake.

11
00:00:45.673 --> 00:00:48.595
He watched me dump all my stuff in a big box.

12
00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:52.938
"Good-bye, Tate," I said, picking up the box.

13
00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:54.900
Tate grinned.

14
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.881
"See you around, Iggy."

15
00:00:58.962 --> 00:01:01.104
I could tell that Tate was happy I was leaving.

16
00:01:02.264 --> 00:01:04.765
But I didn't mind, because I was happy too.

17
00:01:06.506 --> 00:01:09.047
My new room was a tiny space off the kitchen.

18
00:01:10.187 --> 00:01:16.150
Mr. Calabria, the superintendent of our apartment building, had built shelves for all my invention stuff.

19
00:01:18.571 --> 00:01:21.292
Soon he was going to move my bed into the room too.

20
00:01:21.312 --> 00:01:23.133
"Hey, Iggy!"

21
00:01:23.453 --> 00:01:24.053
Tate yelled.

22
00:01:24.073 --> 00:01:25.334
"Come back here!"

23
00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:28.475
"Wow," I thought in surprise.

24
00:01:28.495 --> 00:01:30.736
"Tate misses me already!"

25
00:01:32.072 --> 00:01:33.573
I walked back to Tate's room.

26
00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.194
"What do you want?"

27
00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:36.054
I asked.

28
00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:39.216
"You forgot something," said Tate.

29
00:01:39.957 --> 00:01:43.199
He pointed under his desk.

30
00:01:43.219 --> 00:01:45.440
I looked, but I couldn't see anything.

31
00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.043
"There's a broken crayon under there," Tate said.

32
00:01:51.023 --> 00:01:54.946
I looked again and spotted a tiny piece of broken crayon.

33
00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:58.528
It was from the automatic coloring machine I'd invented.

34
00:01:59.476 --> 00:02:01.958
I picked it up and then went to the door.

35
00:02:02.758 --> 00:02:05.059
Mr. Calabria was here to move my bed.

36
00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.222
I was still setting up my new room when Mom got home.

37
00:02:09.242 --> 00:02:13.764
"I'm so tired from shopping," she said.

38
00:02:13.784 --> 00:02:18.627
"After I put these groceries away, I'm going to sit down with a good book."

39
00:02:20.828 --> 00:02:23.570
Just then someone knocked on our apartment door.

40
00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:27.452
It was my friend Molly, who lives across the hall.

41
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.182
Her little brother, Caswell, was with her.

42
00:02:30.202 --> 00:02:33.064
"Hi, Iggy," she said.

43
00:02:33.084 --> 00:02:34.966
"How's your new room?"

44
00:02:34.986 --> 00:02:38.489
"I'm almost all moved in," I said.

45
00:02:38.509 --> 00:02:39.810
"Come and see!"

46
00:02:43.513 --> 00:02:44.934
I showed them my new room.

47
00:02:44.954 --> 00:02:49.498
"I'm going to think up great inventions here.

48
00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:51.920
My next invention will be healthy candy.

49
00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:53.361
You two can help."

50
00:02:55.263 --> 00:02:56.224
Molly made a face.

51
00:02:57.068 --> 00:02:59.089
"Who wants to eat healthy candy?"

52
00:03:00.049 --> 00:03:02.610
"We're not going to eat it," I explained.

53
00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.571
"We're going to sell it!

54
00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.112
Moms will buy it for their kids."

55
00:03:09.753 --> 00:03:11.074
I went back into the kitchen.

56
00:03:11.094 --> 00:03:15.936
"Mom, can we use some frozen vegetables for my new invention?"

57
00:03:15.956 --> 00:03:18.577
"Okay," she said.

58
00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.658
"But don't make a mess."

59
00:03:20.678 --> 00:03:23.719
"I won't," I promised.

60
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.620
Then I got busy.

61
00:03:27.276 --> 00:03:31.098
First I took three bags of frozen vegetables out of the freezer.

62
00:03:31.979 --> 00:03:34.480
There were lima beans, peas, and broccoli.

63
00:03:36.121 --> 00:03:39.162
Next I dumped the vegetables on a platter in my room.

64
00:03:40.323 --> 00:03:42.144
The broccoli was all stuck together.

65
00:03:44.005 --> 00:03:46.046
We had to use a hammer to break it apart.

66
00:03:46.066 --> 00:03:48.207
"This is fun!"

67
00:03:48.607 --> 00:03:51.069
said Caswell, pounding the frozen broccoli.

68
00:03:51.089 --> 00:03:54.250
"But how are we going to make candy?"

69
00:03:54.691 --> 00:03:55.431
asked Molly.

70
00:03:55.451 --> 00:03:57.929
"You'll see," I told her.

71
00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:01.872
I went into the kitchen and got a stool.

72
00:04:03.053 --> 00:04:05.495
Then I climbed up and got a bottle from the cupboard.

73
00:04:06.636 --> 00:04:08.758
Its label said "Chocolate Syrup."

74
00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:13.802
"Now," I said, as I came back into my room.

75
00:04:13.822 --> 00:04:17.526
"We'll pour the syrup over the frozen vegetables.

76
00:04:18.486 --> 00:04:19.688
Then the syrup will freeze.

77
00:04:20.869 --> 00:04:23.931
The candy will be just like a chocolate-coated ice-cream cone!"

78
00:04:26.188 --> 00:04:30.831
"But the candy will still taste like vegetables," Molly pointed out.

79
00:04:30.851 --> 00:04:32.492
"Who cares?"

80
00:04:32.973 --> 00:04:33.773
said Caswell.

81
00:04:33.793 --> 00:04:35.695
"Let's start pouring!"

82
00:04:37.236 --> 00:04:39.417
We all took turns pouring the syrup.

83
00:04:41.118 --> 00:04:45.041
Caswell tried to be careful, but he got syrup all over his face.

84
00:04:46.722 --> 00:04:49.364
In fact, he got syrup all over everything.

85
00:04:50.465 --> 00:04:52.366
That was when Mom walked into my room.

86
00:04:52.386 --> 00:04:54.908
"Iggy!" she cried.

87
00:04:55.913 --> 00:04:57.141
"What do you think you're doing?"
